{
 "id": "053-salincak-sirasi",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "My Turn on the Swing",
 "theme": "Waiting for your turn and sharing turns fairly",
 "blurb": "Two swings in the park, three friends. Ela gets very cross, but she takes a deep breath and finds an idea: “Five swings each, then we swap!”",
 "voiceNames": {
  "ela": "Ela",
  "can": "Can",
  "deniz": "Deniz"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "It was a sunny morning. Can and Deniz were on the swings. Whoooo, whoooo! Can shouted: “My feet touched the clouds!” Ela came running. “I want to swing too!”",
   "hits": {
    "ela": {
     "say": "I want to swing too!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "My feet touched the clouds!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Whoooo, whoooo!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ela!",
   "ask": "What do you like riding on most at the park?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 12,
     "fx": "ruzgar"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "“It's my turn!” said Ela. “I've only just got on!” said Can. “Me too!” said Deniz. Ela got very cross. Her cheeks went red, and she squeezed her fists tight. Stomp, stomp, she stamped her foot on the ground!",
   "hits": {
    "ela": {
     "say": "My cheeks are burning! My fists are squeezed tight!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "But I've only just got on!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "I've only just got on too!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ela!",
   "ask": "How is Ela feeling? How can you tell from her cheeks, her hands and her feet?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ela stopped. She took a deep breath. In, like smelling a flower, and out, like blowing a candle: fwooo! Her cheeks cooled down. An idea popped into her head!",
   "hits": {
    "ela": {
     "say": "Fwooo… I feel calmer now."
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Ahh! Ela has calmed down.",
    "msg": "You breathed together!"
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Ela will do?",
    "res": "Both are good ways! Let's see.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "Talk to Can"
     },
     {
      "l": "Wait on the bench"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Smell the flower, blow the candle!",
   "ask": "What do you do when you're cross? Let's try it with Ela: smell the flower, blow the candle!"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ela looked into Can's eyes and smiled: “Let's swing five times. Then we swap!” “Okay!” said Can. Ela waited and counted: “One, two, three, four, five!”",
   "hits": {
    "ela": {
     "say": "Let's swing five times!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "Okay! You count, Ela!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Five times for me too!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Five! Time to swap!",
    "msg": "You counted to five!"
   },
   "hint": "You count too!",
   "ask": "What idea did Ela have? Can you count to five on your fingers?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can hopped off the swing. “Here you go, Ela, it's your turn!” he said. Ela walked to the swing. Step, step, one more step!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Here you go, Ela, it's your turn!"
    },
    "ela": {
     "say": "Thank you, Can!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Come on, Ela, come!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Ela reached the swing!",
    "msg": "It's Ela's turn!",
    "say": "Step, step, one more step!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ela so she walks!",
   "ask": "How did Ela feel when Can gave her his turn? What do you say when you want a turn?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ela swung: whoooo! Can counted. At five, Ela got off. Then Can, then Ela again! The turns went round and round. “Everyone gets a turn!” said Deniz.",
   "hits": {
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Everyone gets a turn!"
    },
    "ela": {
     "say": "Whoooo! I feel like I'm flying!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "Then it's you, Deniz!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Deniz!",
   "ask": "Why did everyone get a turn? Who do you take turns with?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 2,
     "fx": "ruzgar"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "SBAB5 Social Participation (domain skill): joins in the shared game at the park; notices that two swings are not enough for three friends and suggests a rule that gives everyone a turn (“Five swings each, then we swap”).",
   "MAB.1 Counting rhythmically and by sight (36–48 month adaptation: counts forward by ones from 1 to 5, finds how many by counting): counts the swings together with Ela, “one, two, three, four, five”; notices that the last number said is what changes the turn.",
   "TAKB.1 Managing the speaking process (secondary): instead of shouting for what she wants, looks her friend in the eye and says her suggestion in a calm voice; waits for her friend's answer.",
   "SDB2.1 Communication and D1 Justice: sets up a rule that gives everyone an equal turn; says “Here you go, it's your turn!” to the next friend."
  ],
  "once": [
   "Point to the swing on the cover: “How many swings are there? How many children? What do you think will happen?”",
   "Ask: “Have you ever waited for a turn with a toy? How did you feel while you waited?” Listen to the answers without judging."
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "On page 2, point to Ela's cheeks and fists: “What happened in Ela's body when she got cross?” Squeeze your fists with the children, then let them go loose.",
   "On page 3, touch the flower and the candle and breathe twice with Ela: smell the flower (in through the nose), blow the candle (out through the mouth, “fwooo”). For the prediction question, say that both choices are good.",
   "On page 4, show that Ela counted while she waited; as you touch the number cards, count all together with a rhythm: “One, two, three, four, five!” Rock your body once for each number, as if swinging."
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "Have the child tell the events in order: Ela got cross → she took a breath → she suggested five swings each → Can gave her his turn → everyone got a turn.",
   "Ask: “What did Ela do when she was cross? What do you try when you're cross?” Together, list ways like taking a breath, talking it over or telling a grown-up.",
   "Find sentences together for asking for a turn: “Can I have a go too?”, “Shall we do five each and take turns?”, “Here you go, it's your turn!”"
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "Swing Five Times, Pass the Turn",
   "sure": "15 min",
   "materyal": "Number cards from 1 to 5, a chair or cushion (the “swing”), some calm music",
   "adim": [
    "The chair becomes the class “swing”. Say the rule: “We swing five times on the swing, then we swap turns.”",
    "One child sits on the chair and rocks forwards and backwards; the children waiting count all together, showing the number cards one by one: “One, two, three, four, five!”",
    "At “Five!” the sitting child gets up and says to the next one, “Here you go, it's your turn!”; the next child answers, “Thank you!”",
    "To finish, ask: “How did you feel while you waited? How did you feel when your turn came?” The children show it with their faces."
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "Why did Ela get cross? What happened to her cheeks and hands when she was cross?",
   "What did Ela do to calm down? Let's try it together!",
   "What idea did Ela have? How many times did they swing?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Five Each at Home",
   "d": "Pick a toy that is hard to share with your child or their sibling. While taking turns with the toy, slowly count to five together; at “Five!” the toy passes to the next person. As the turn changes, practise saying “Here you go, it's your turn!” and “Thank you!”"
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read “My Turn on the Swing.” There are two swings and three friends at the park; when it isn't her turn, Ela gets very cross, takes a deep breath to calm down and comes up with the idea “Five swings each, then we swap!” The story supports waiting for a turn, showing feelings in calm ways and counting rhythmically to five. At home, you can try this rule by counting to five together while taking turns with toys."
 },
